What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_pending_mask
Date: September 2026
Contact: CJFS research fork maintainers
Description:
 Experimental observation groups: 0 disabled, 1 basic, 3 basic plus ranges.
 Pending settings are applied by collect_apply=1 while stopped. Only ordered
 data, internal-journal, non-FC writable ext4 is supported.

What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_pending_sample_every
What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_pending_memory_bytes
Date: September 2026
Description:
 Deterministic block-identity sampling denominator (1..65536) for ranges only,
 and preallocated history budget (1..64 MiB). Basic counts are not sampled.
 History collisions and missing baselines use full-image estimates.

What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_apply
What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_start
What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_phase
What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_stop
Date: September 2026
Description:
 Apply drains and installs pending settings while stopped. Start syncs/drains,
 resets and starts a session. Phase is 0 (workload), changed once by writing 1
 to mark drain. Stop requires phase 1 and syncs/drains before stopping probes.
 Write 1 to apply/start/stop. Quiesce workload writers before phase/stop.
 CJFS policy application is rejected while collecting. Controls require admin
 capability and protect mount lifetime. Aborted sessions are invalid; unmount
 releases the collector. These controls never change the journal log format.

What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_status
What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_workload
What: /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/collect_drain
Date: September 2026
Description:
 Read-only newline-separated key/integer snapshots, schema 1. Status contains
 session, effective configuration, capacity, timestamps and abort state.
 Phase files contain accepted BIO write volumes, journal extent intersections,
 unclassified nonjournal bytes, staged metadata/control counts, existing CJFS
 copy/transaction events and hypothetical range encoding counts. Atomic
 counters are approximate while active and frozen after stop.
 Range estimates compare normalized logged images, not disk baselines. They
 are not a recovery format. Full fallback applies to unavailable histories.
 Summing phases accounts for boundary-crossing transactions. Detailed metric
 semantics and the encoder assumptions are in jrnl-poc/cjfs/live/WORK-VOLUME.md
 in the accompanying experiment repository.
